Test file: internal/platform/httputil/logging_sink_test.go
Helper:    a fakeSink struct with mu-protected []*models.APICallLog buffer, configurable
           captureBodies bool, optional enqueueDelay time.Duration, and Snapshot()/Len() helpers.

T01 SinkRecordsSuccessfulGet — single GET maps cleanly to a single api_call_logs row
  GIVEN  httptest server returning 200 "ok" at /v1/users
         client := httputil.NewClient(httputil.ClientConfig{Name: "example-api", Sink: sink,
                                                            EnableLogging: true})
  WHEN   client.Get(srv.URL + "/v1/users")
  THEN   sink.Len() == 1 AND entry has:
             service       == "example-api"          (from ClientConfig.Name -> LoggedTransport.Name)
             http_method   == "GET"
             endpoint      == srv.URL + "/v1/users"   (no query, no redaction needed)
             status_code   == 200
             duration_ms   >  0
             vehicle_id    IS NULL                   (no vehicle context for generic outbound)
             error_message == ""
  ANCHOR service tag inherited from ClientConfig.Name; Sink injection working; exactly one
         sink entry per round-trip.

T02 ServiceTagPropagatesFromClientConfigName — Name flows through transport chain
  GIVEN  three clients constructed with Names "eia-api", "geocoder", "tesla-internal"
  WHEN   each issues one request
  THEN   the three sink entries have service tags matching their respective ClientConfig.Name.
         No entry has an empty service tag.
  ANCHOR ClientConfig.Name == LoggedTransport.Name == APICallLog.Service. This is the only
         supported way to label outbound calls; tests forbid any other source.

T03 NoDoubleRecord_TeslaAdapterUsesSingleSource — exactly one persistence path per Tesla call
  GIVEN  a Tesla-shaped client constructed with both:
             httputil.NewClient(ClientConfig{Name: "tesla-api", Sink: nil, EnableLogging: true})
             AND tesla.SetLogCallback(cb) where cb forwards into the same sink.
  WHEN   one outbound Tesla request completes
  THEN   sink.Len() == 1 (NOT 2).
  AND    asserts the symmetric guarantee: when Sink is non-nil for tesla-api AND
         SetLogCallback is also installed, the test FAILS LOUDLY (sink.Len() == 2). This is
         a regression guard: Prompt 12 must document in code comments that exactly one of
         {Sink, SetLogCallback} is installed per adapter. Production wiring keeps
         SetLogCallback for Tesla (it has decoded bodies + 401-refresh retry context) and
         uses Sink for every other outbound adapter.
  ANCHOR no double-record / single source of truth per outbound HTTP call.

T04 RedactsSensitiveQueryParameters — endpoint stored in api_call_logs is sanitized
  GIVEN  request URL ?api_key=SUPERSECRET&token=abc&secret=xyz&password=hunter2&visible=ok
  WHEN   round-trip completes
  THEN   sink entry endpoint contains visible=ok AND contains "REDACTED" four times
         (api_key, token, secret, password). The original SUPERSECRET / abc / xyz / hunter2
         strings MUST NOT appear anywhere in the persisted endpoint or any other field.
         Pattern parity: redaction matches (?i)token|key|secret|password (the cookie variant
         is header-only; query-side parity covers token|key|secret|password). The existing
         sanitizeURL() helper in logging.go must be extended to also redact "password"; today
         it only redacts key|token|secret. Prompt 12 will add the missing case so the inbound
         and outbound persisted endpoints share the same redaction superset.
  ANCHOR REDACTED placeholder + redact term + parity with inbound middleware regex.

T05 RedactsSensitiveHeaders_WhenBodyCaptureEnabled — header capture parity with inbound
  GIVEN  Sink.CaptureBodies() == true; request carries Authorization, Cookie, X-Api-Key headers
  WHEN   round-trip completes
  THEN   the persisted request_headers map has Authorization=REDACTED, Cookie=REDACTED,
         X-Api-Key=REDACTED; non-sensitive headers (User-Agent, Accept) are preserved verbatim.
  ANCHOR REDACTED appears in headers; same regex as inbound (?i)token|key|secret|password|cookie.

T06 BodyCaptureOptIn_DefaultOff — no bodies persisted when sink opts out
  GIVEN  Sink.CaptureBodies() == false (the default); POST with non-empty JSON body; server
         responds 200 with non-empty JSON
  WHEN   round-trip completes
  THEN   sink entry request_body IS NULL AND response_body IS NULL. Other fields populated.
  ANCHOR CaptureBodies opt-in behavior, default is off.

T07 BodyCaptureOptIn_TruncatesAt10KB — opt-in capture respects 10 KB cap
  GIVEN  Sink.CaptureBodies() == true; request body 12 KB; response body 25 KB
  WHEN   round-trip completes
  THEN   sink entry request_body length == 10 KB (10240 bytes) AND ends with the inbound
         truncation marker; response_body length == 10 KB AND ends with the truncation marker.
         Marker text matches the cappedBuffer marker used by the inbound middleware so a single
         downstream parser can detect truncation regardless of direction.
  AND    body capture does NOT corrupt the bytes seen by the caller: the test reads the full
         response body via resp.Body and asserts byte-for-byte equality with the server-emitted
         payload (TeeReader preserves the stream).
  ANCHOR body capture truncated to 10 KB; non-destructive to caller's byte stream.

T08 NetworkErrorIsRecorded — connection refused / DNS failure path persists
  GIVEN  client targeting an unreachable address (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:1/ for connection
         refused, AND a separate sub-test targeting http://does-not-exist.invalid./ for
         DNS NXDOMAIN)
  WHEN   round-trip returns an error
  THEN   sink.Len() == 1 per attempt AND the entry has:
             status_code   == 0
             error_message != ""                (substring "connection refused" or "no such host")
             duration_ms   >= 0                 (network error path may be sub-millisecond)
             response_body IS NULL
             endpoint      matches the redacted URL
  ANCHOR status_code=0 and network error / connection refused / DNS recorded with non-empty
         error_message.

T09 NilSinkIsSafe_PreservesLegacyZerologBehavior — backward-compat with existing call sites
  GIVEN  httputil.NewClient(ClientConfig{Name: "noop", Sink: nil, EnableLogging: true})
  WHEN   round-trip completes (success path AND error path, two sub-tests)
  THEN   no panic; the existing zerolog "outbound request" / "outbound response" / "outbound
         request failed" log lines are still emitted (verified by capturing log.Logger output
         exactly as the existing TestLoggedTransport_* tests do); no sink interaction occurs
         (the test uses a tracking sink that fails the test if any method is called).
  ANCHOR nil Sink => no panic; legacy behavior unchanged.

T10 SinkCallIsNonBlocking_SlowSinkDoesNotIncreaseLatency — async contract holds
  GIVEN  fakeSink.enqueueDelay = 250ms (Enqueue blocks for 250ms when called synchronously)
         AND a control client with sink == nil
  WHEN   each client issues one round-trip against the same fast (200 OK, <5ms) httptest server
  THEN   wallclock latency observed by the caller for the sink-enabled client is within
         +5ms of the control client's latency (definitely << 250ms). This proves the sink call
         is non-blocking from the round-trip's perspective — either fired in a goroutine or
         submitted to a buffered channel by the production APICallLogger implementation.
  ANCHOR no panic / sink is non-blocking; round-trip latency unaffected by slow sink.

T11 LayeringRule_HttputilDoesNotImportDatabase — package-level static assertion
  GIVEN  the source tree of internal/platform/httputil
  WHEN   the test walks all *.go files (including _test.go) and parses imports via go/parser
         + go/token (build tag-aware via go/build)
  THEN   no file imports "github.com/ev-dev-labs/teslasync/internal/database" (or any
         subpackage thereof). The assertion fails loudly with the offending file:line if any
         such import appears in the future.
  AND    a companion sub-test asserts no import of "github.com/ev-dev-labs/teslasync/internal/api"
         in the production (non _test.go) files of internal/platform/httputil. Test files MAY
         import internal/api only to use the APICallLogger interface in integration tests; the
         preferred form is to import only internal/models and define a local fake.
  ANCHOR layering: internal/platform/httputil must not import internal/database; the rule is
         enforced as a unit test, not just by convention.

T12 PreservesExistingZerologLines — additive sink does not regress current tests
  GIVEN  the three pre-existing tests TestLoggedTransport_Success, TestLoggedTransport_Error,
         and TestLoggedTransport_SanitizesAPIKey
  WHEN   re-run after Prompt 12's changes
  THEN   all three pass unmodified. The sink path is additive and does not alter the shape or
         level of zerolog output.
  ANCHOR existing zerolog log lines preserved; sink is purely additive.

T13 EndpointIncludesPathAndRedactedQuery — full URL captured, not just path
  GIVEN  request to https://example.test:8443/v1/users/42?token=abc&filter=active
  WHEN   round-trip completes (test uses an httptest TLS server; example.test resolves via
         a custom transport rewriting host)
  THEN   sink entry endpoint == "https://example.test:8443/v1/users/42?token=REDACTED&filter=active"
         (scheme + host:port + path + redacted query, all preserved).
  ANCHOR endpoint precisely formatted; REDACTED replaces the sensitive value.

T14 VehicleIDPropagationViaContext — optional vehicle correlation
  GIVEN  ctx := httputil.WithVehicleID(parent, 42); request issued with that ctx
         (the helper httputil.WithVehicleID + ContextVehicleID is part of Prompt 12's surface)
  WHEN   round-trip completes
  THEN   sink entry vehicle_id == 42.
  AND    the no-context variant (T01) verified vehicle_id IS NULL. Both must pass.
  ANCHOR vehicle_id correlation flows through ctx; absent ctx => NULL.

T15 ConcurrentRoundTripsRecordOneEntryEach — concurrency safety
  GIVEN  100 concurrent goroutines each issuing one GET via the same client + sink
  WHEN   all complete
  THEN   sink.Len() == 100; each entry has a distinct duration_ms (most likely; allow
         duplicates as long as count is exact); no data race detected under -race.
  ANCHOR no panic / single source of truth holds under concurrency.

